  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP/DCPSF Sudan 2018-23 - Darfur Fund, 2014 - 17 , UNDP Sudan</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UNDP/DCPSF Sudan 2018-23</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">DCPSF &#xe4;r en givarfond som hanteras av UNDP. Fondens strategi &#xe4;r att st&#xf6;dja projekt p&#xe5; gr&#xe4;srotsniv&#xe5; som arbetar med de grundl&#xe4;ggande orsakerna till konflikterna p&#xe5; lokal niv&#xe5; i Darfur. Detta gjordes tidigare med syftet att komplettera &#xf6;vergripande fredsprocesser, men detta syfte har i praktiken ersatts med det f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntade resultatet: &quot;St&#xe4;rkt f&#xf6;rm&#xe5;ga att genom lokala fredsinitiativ f&#xf6;rebygga konflikter och &#xe5;stadkomma f&#xf6;rsoning i Darfur&quot;. Projekten under DCPSF p&#xe5;g&#xe5;r parallellt med p&#xe5;g&#xe5;ende humanit&#xe4;ra insatser, d&#xe4;r samverkan fr&#xe4;mst sker genom koordering och utbyte av information om l&#xe4;get i Darfur. DCPSF utg&#xf6;r ett av de f&#xe5; program som st&#xf6;djer fredsbyggande p&#xe5; lokal niv&#xe5; i Darfur.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Darfur Community and Peace Building Fund (DCPSF), phase 2 (2011-2020). A community driven peace and reconciliation initiative. UNDP administers the fund which aims to foster dialogue and funding of small scale peace building initiatives at community level. The support is a second tranche for phase 2, in line with the Results Strategy for Sudan, 2014-2017.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of Darfur Community Peace and Stability Fund (DCPSF) is to improve security and stabilization of communities affected by conflict through utilization of effective conflict management mechanisms, peace dividends and support to peace infrastructures and durable solutions that augment peaceful coexistance and social cohesion.&#xa0;
The DCPSF has four expected outputs:
1) Community-based conflict resolution and reconciliation mechanisms are in use and working effectively to resolve conflict;
2) Peace dividends for community interdependence and co-existance are delivered;
3) Women&apos;s organisations, including those representing pastoralists women, empowered to meaningfully participate in local and state-level peacebuilding platforms;
4) Improved networking, coordination and learning between local and state-level peacebuilding institutions.</narrative>
  </description>
